@@ -0,0 +1,132 @@
+# tvOS Build System Support
+
+This document describes how the engine build system was extended to support
+`et build --config tvos_debug_sim_unopt_arm64` targeting the Apple TV simulator.
+
+## Files modified
+
+All modifications live inside the engine tree. Changes are scoped to the
+build system; no iOS engine source was touched.
+
+- `engine/src/build/mac/darwin_sdk.py`
+  Added `appletvos` and `appletvsimulator` to the supported `SDKS` list.
+- `engine/src/build/config/darwin/darwin_sdk.gni`
+  Declared new tvOS GN args (`is_tvos`, `use_tvos_simulator`,
+  `tvos_deployment_target`, `tvos_sdk_path`, `tvos_device_sdk_path`,
+  `tvos_simulator_sdk_path`, `tvos_device_platform_path`,
+  `tvos_simulator_platform_path`). Added SDK path resolution: when
+  `is_tvos && is_ios` the effective `ios_sdk_path`/`ios_platform_path` are
+  routed at the tvOS SDK/platform, which keeps the existing toolchains and
+  downstream iOS-tree references working unchanged.
+- `engine/src/build/toolchain/mac/BUILD.gn`
+  Added three new `mac_toolchain()` definitions (only active when
+  `is_tvos`): `tvos_clang_arm64` (device), `tvos_clang_arm_sim` (simulator
+  arm64), `tvos_clang_x64_sim` (simulator x64). Each uses the tvOS SDK and
+  the `-mappletvos-version-min=` / `-mappletvsimulator-version-min=` flag.
+- `engine/src/build/config/BUILDCONFIG.gn`
+  When `is_ios && is_tvos`, selects one of the new tvOS toolchains as the
+  default, instead of the `ios_clang_*` toolchains.
+- `engine/src/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn`
+  Emits `--target=arm64-apple-tvos-simulator` (or device equivalent) as the
+  Clang target triple when `is_tvos`. iOS behaviour unchanged.
+- `engine/src/build/config/darwin/BUILD.gn`
+  Emits the correct Swift `-target` triplet
+  (`arm64-apple-tvos14.0-simulator`) when `is_tvos`.
+- `engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/darwin/ios/BUILD.gn`
+  Removed the local `declare_args { is_tvos }` block (now a global arg in
+  `darwin_sdk.gni`).
+- `engine/src/flutter/tools/gn`
+  Added `--tvos` and `--tvos-simulator` argparse flags. `--tvos` implies
+  `target_os=ios`; `--tvos-simulator` additionally implies `--simulator`
+  and `--tvos`. Emits `is_tvos` and `use_tvos_simulator` into the GN args
+  dict. Added `AppleTVOS`/`AppleTVSimulator` prefixes to `setup_apple_sdks`
+  so the `//flutter/prebuilts/SDKs` and `//flutter/prebuilts/Platforms`
+  symlinks are consumed. Named the output directory `out/tvos_...` so it
+  does not collide with an iOS build at the same runtime/cpu.
+- `engine/src/flutter/ci/builders/local_engine.json`
+  Added a new `macos/tvos_debug_sim_unopt_arm64` builder entry mirroring
+  the existing `macos/ios_debug_sim_unopt_arm64` entry but passing
+  `--tvos --tvos-simulator` to `tools/gn` and naming the ninja config
+  `tvos_debug_sim_unopt_arm64`.
+
+## New GN args
+
+Declared in `build/config/darwin/darwin_sdk.gni`:
+
+| Arg | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `is_tvos` | `false` | Global toggle: when true, the iOS target tree builds a tvOS-flavored Flutter.framework. |
+| `use_tvos_simulator` | `true` | Mirrors `use_ios_simulator` for the tvOS variant. |
+| `tvos_deployment_target` | `"14.0"` | Passed via `-mappletv[os\|simulator]-version-min` and in the Swift triple. |
+| `tvos_sdk_path` | `""` | Effective tvOS SDK (set by darwin_sdk.gni from the device/simulator path). |
+| `tvos_device_sdk_path` | `""` | Path to AppleTVOS SDK. |
+| `tvos_simulator_sdk_path` | `""` | Path to AppleTVSimulator SDK. |
+| `tvos_device_platform_path` | `""` | Path to AppleTVOS.platform. |
+| `tvos_simulator_platform_path` | `""` | Path to AppleTVSimulator.platform. |
+
+## How to invoke a tvOS build
+
+```bash
+cd engine/src/flutter
+./bin/et build --config tvos_debug_sim_unopt_arm64
+```
+
+The build output lives at `engine/src/out/tvos_debug_sim_unopt_arm64/`.
+
+The equivalent raw gn invocation is:
+
+```bash
+python3 tools/gn \
+    --tvos --tvos-simulator --simulator-cpu=arm64 \
+    --runtime-mode debug --unoptimized --no-stripped --no-lto \
+    --xcode-symlinks --rbe --no-goma
+```
+
+## First-compile result
+
+**Build-system wiring: WORKING.** GN generation completes cleanly and ninja
+selects the new `tvos_clang_arm_sim` toolchain, emits the correct sysroot
+(`AppleTVSimulator26.4.sdk`), and drives clang with `--target=arm64-apple-tvos-simulator`
+and `-mappletvsimulator-version-min=14.0`. Skia compiles clean. Roughly 293 of
+7046 targets built before ninja stopped on the first iOS-specific source-level
+tvOS-incompatibility.
+
+**Compile failures observed (source-level, not build-system level):**
+
+1. `shell/platform/darwin/ios/framework/Headers/FlutterSceneLifeCycle.h:96:35` – `'UIApplicationShortcutItem' is unavailable: not available on tvOS`
+2. `shell/platform/darwin/ios/framework/Headers/FlutterSceneLifeCycle.h:198:35` – same, second reference
+3. `../out/tvos_debug_sim_unopt_arm64/Flutter.framework/Headers/FlutterSceneLifeCycle.h:96:35` – same (header copied into framework)
+4. `../out/tvos_debug_sim_unopt_arm64/Flutter.framework/Headers/FlutterSceneLifeCycle.h:198:35` – same
+5. `shell/platform/darwin/ios/InternalFlutterSwift-Bridging-Header.h:8:9` – `could not build module 'Flutter'` (cascade from #1–4)
+6. `shell/platform/darwin/common/framework/Source/Logger.swift:60:3` – `'self.init' isn't called on all paths before returning from initializer` (pre-existing Swift code branching that is valid on iOS but exhaustive-check failure when the `#if` arm picks a non-initializing path on tvOS)
+
+All of these are source-code tvOS porting issues, not build-system problems:
+the toolchain, SDK, and flag plumbing are correct.
+
+## Known limitations
+
+- The `is_tvos` variant still has `is_ios == true` at the GN layer. Downstream
+  `BUILD.gn` files must explicitly check `!is_tvos` if they wish to exclude
+  iOS-only code. The ios/BUILD.gn already gates WebKit/IOKit correctly, but
+  other iOS-only APIs referenced from headers (e.g.
+  `UIApplicationShortcutItem`, `UIMenuBuilder`) surface as compile errors
+  inside public framework headers and will need to be conditionally
+  `API_UNAVAILABLE(tvos)`-guarded or excluded from the tvOS header copy set.
+- `tvos_deployment_target` defaults to `"14.0"`; adjust as needed for the
+  target fleet.
+- The `ios_clang_arm` toolchain (iOS device arm) is currently not built for
+  tvOS — a full tvOS device target needs `tvos_clang_arm64` which is wired
+  but untested (no `--tvos` + `--no-simulator` build path exercised; one
+  could add a `tvos_debug_arm64` builder when needed).
+- Swift bridging-header compilation inherits the `Flutter.h` umbrella header,
+  so any single iOS-only symbol in a public header breaks the whole Swift
+  module build. Source-level fix will be needed for the
+  `FlutterSceneLifeCycle.h` hits above.
+
+## Next concrete action
+
+Port `shell/platform/darwin/ios/framework/Headers/FlutterSceneLifeCycle.h`
+(and the copied framework header) by gating `UIApplicationShortcutItem`
+references behind `#if !TARGET_OS_TV` (or annotating the selectors
+`API_UNAVAILABLE(tvos)`). Then rebuild; the next few errors will reveal what
+else in the umbrella header needs gating.
